{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nBinding persistence shares `binding_store.py` with lifecycle policy. Extraction is unsafe until byte layout, load rules, unconditional save behavior, and ordered partial-state failures have direct oracles.\n\n## Outcome\nCreate `BindingRepository` as the sole owner of live, retired, rotation, and alert files. It retains the original dictionaries, exact serialization, load behavior, and current unconditional save boundary. No facade cutover or new dirty gate occurs in this task.\n\n## Plan\n1. Start with direct failing tests over legacy/unknown-field fixtures, construction with no eager write, unconditional save, and exact sorted/indented/trailing-newline bytes.\n2. Implement path ownership, open typed views over original dictionaries, tempfile cleanup, and per-file `os.replace`. Current-code oracles are `BindingStore._load`, `_load_retired`, `_save_retired`, `_alert`, `save`, `_retire`, and `get_rotation.save` on the reviewed base.\n3. Pin the existing corruption contract: corrupt live JSON raises `ValueError` and preserves the file; corrupt retired JSON returns empty, preserves the file, and attempts a deduped alert; alert failure is swallowed.\n4. Pin exact persistence cuts:\n   - rotation tempfile/write/replace failure: rotation stays old; live is replaced with new bytes retaining inline `last_get_pass`; failure is swallowed.\n   - next-save recovery after that cut: remove the injected failure, call save again, and assert the rotation sidecar converges from retained inline `last_get_pass` before live replacement.\n   - live tempfile/write/replace failure after successful rotation: rotation is new; live stays old; temp is cleaned; failure raises.\n   - retired tempfile/write/replace failure: retired and live stay old; temp is cleaned; failure raises.\n   - live replacement failure during retirement: retired is new; live stays old; temp is cleaned; failure raises.\n   - alert persistence failure after a successful state write changes no state-file result and is swallowed.\n5. Keep the current retired-first and rotation-before-live order. Make no multi-file atomicity, journal, eager-load rewrite, deep-copy, publication, or write-elision claim.\n\n## Testing\nUse real temporary files and injected cuts at each named operation. Assert exact surviving bytes, cleanup, and exception outcome. Add a two-save rotation test: fail the first sidecar write, verify the inline floor survives in live, allow the second sidecar write, then verify sidecar/live convergence. The current reviewed functions above are the characterization source; captured fixtures make the oracle durable.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Legacy and unknown-field fixtures round-trip to byte-identical sorted/indented/newline JSON, and construction performs no eager write.\n- [ ] Calling save without an in-memory change still attempts rotation persistence before live replacement.\n- [ ] Corrupt live state fails closed; corrupt retired state fails open with best-effort alerting.\n- [ ] Rotation persistence failure leaves rotation old and live new with the inline floor, without raising.\n- [ ] After one injected rotation failure, the next successful save writes the retained inline floor to the sidecar before live replacement; verified by the two-save fault/recovery test.\n- [ ] Retired persistence failure leaves retired/live old and raises.\n- [ ] Live persistence failure leaves live old, retains any earlier successful sidecar/retired write, cleans its temp, and raises.\n- [ ] Alert persistence failure is swallowed and does not alter the successful state-file result.\n\n## Out of scope\nFacade delegation, lifecycle extraction, tickets publication, recovery cutover, and dirty/write-elision optimization remain outside this task."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787030909531960001,"uuid":"6515c9fa-da2e-40d2-a173-8b94b0f3356b"}